{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he added yet more.</b> Meaning, that he sent the first ones and added others to them, and this is what is also to be examined precisely in the expression <b>from these</b>, for it does not say מֵהֶם, to say that [some] of those first brought in the mission are still together with those added over them. And his intention in this was that he not contradict his first statement, in which he had attributed the matter to the insufficiency of the envoys — that they had reproached him to his face." "<b>Further,</b> the expression <b>וַיֹּסֶף</b> intends that he added to the first count, such that if the first ones were three, in the second count he sent four or more. And this would not be conveyed if he had said ״וַיִּשְׁלַח עוֹד שָׂרִים רַבִּים״ etc., for I would have said that he says ״רַבִּים״ so that you not think he sent fewer than the first count. And his saying <b>מֵאֵלֶּה</b> refers back to the word ״נִכְבָּדִים״; therefore it says ״וַיֹּסֶף״."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:36.998728815Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}